#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aa83bc8-7a74-540d-88db-e19eaa52bbbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336849} {:answer/id #uuid "5123fc09-d68f-5a66-9cb5-ab5d772b00a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336850} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc53cb3-ac2c-5c40-b16b-a2c433f70813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\le x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336851} {:answer/id #uuid "9df67623-03d3-57a8-b0d0-37e2b6c1bff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336852} {:answer/id #uuid "a5e32ab7-f1fa-5556-9c14-764d7b51e7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\le x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cc53cb3-ac2c-5c40-b16b-a2c433f70813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\le x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336851} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d486a9-0c77-56cb-a5d9-cb60b5077939" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb1e01eb-14f1-577c-a4b7-0a54f287effc" :question/math-academy-id "q-142314" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+x-12\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/eda4704129b905a10e379254dfd6d1ff07d593d7f97bbc6126e9d27bfec2f9f2.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-4\\le x\\le 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e69649ce-42f9-5691-923a-d247fdd42a5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69649ce-42f9-5691-923a-d247fdd42a5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336856} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7196d3d-50f2-5a3e-855d-aedbdfff5577" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f93f7865-bb56-5650-a8e1-210b3358e2a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f93f7865-bb56-5650-a8e1-210b3358e2a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336858} :answer-field/id #uuid "0486b523-ad57-5ead-824b-4856aee7f54b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "919706fc-13ef-523e-8d75-285c6e670a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "919706fc-13ef-523e-8d75-285c6e670a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336860} :answer-field/id #uuid "52611d45-624a-5dbc-bf7a-21bde6074b0e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "021dad23-6108-5419-9f6e-96c817c309f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-276404" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $6{x}^{2}+21x\\ge 12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]\\,⋃\\,[${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x & \\ge 12 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}+21x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-3x)+(24x-12) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-1)+12(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ (3x+12)(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ 3(x+4)(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/38c1897ec93625527b48ec689fbd65e9a63056e033fa6a7a0c72473f1188e7ea.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+21x-12\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]⋃[\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6abcce9e-293d-5d3b-b327-abc625edeb44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336863} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c33c78-a992-5bfb-a4ae-52acbb1074d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c33c78-a992-5bfb-a4ae-52acbb1074d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336864} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cede853-9e96-5001-b91f-5676128a5dfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "440795f7-cc0c-5087-b5cf-93b03ee9b058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "440795f7-cc0c-5087-b5cf-93b03ee9b058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336866} :answer-field/id #uuid "a89272e7-ee3e-587f-85dd-97c82980276d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deba747d-4ccd-535e-b601-450eff0af74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deba747d-4ccd-535e-b601-450eff0af74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336868} :answer-field/id #uuid "c862efd6-8a65-5491-8dfa-f778d618caa6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dbdb8111-2a4d-5f07-9e95-10b7d4c127c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-277263" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-7x\\le 0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-7x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-7x & =0 \\\\ x(x-7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=7,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/e7f9e5a051acca0be45340695fd6c2ddcb9d47936cc1f713245bd22d33151c97.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0\\le x\\le 7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efac5182-d12a-5b78-968c-f9aa01f5d7fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efac5182-d12a-5b78-968c-f9aa01f5d7fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336871} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf0d4c-944a-5cf5-881e-dcbc6b721475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b9eb35b-a126-5956-be77-460c5ae3f119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b9eb35b-a126-5956-be77-460c5ae3f119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336873} :answer-field/id #uuid "b868b0e9-7ae0-50f6-8243-7053e9a125f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab6898a8-0c6c-568c-acc9-98203dcb0b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab6898a8-0c6c-568c-acc9-98203dcb0b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336875} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d0a39f-c6f9-59ba-af71-269f2e474f81" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76733b46-8281-5054-9373-31b632e8685f" :question/math-academy-id "q-277667" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}-17x>-2{x}^{2}+45$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,⋃\\,(${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-17x & >-2{x}^{2}+45 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}-17x-45$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-27x)+(10x-45) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-9)+5(2x-9) & =0 \\\\ (3x+5)(2x-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{9}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/f73c9906e6b65d1ddbda91619c7ffbb77408faa0541e2bc16565e0127d334312.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-17x-45>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<-\\frac{5}{3}$ or $x>\\frac{9}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{3})⋃(\\frac{9}{2},\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c13cb2ce-9b12-5979-95e0-b27abfb088d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[MATH: x ∈ (- ∞,-6]∪[1, ∞)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182999} {:answer/id #uuid "c5657a3c-f3d3-5215-a10d-222e7c68febb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[MATH: x ∈ (- ∞, 1]∪[6, ∞)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183000} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1bc666-c1ba-5ce6-9c31-2be31d7cebe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[MATH: x ∈ (- ∞,-1]∪[6, ∞)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183001} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1df24a-8e60-5e10-aff6-59b4471ec881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 1, 6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183002} {:answer/id #uuid "6f145a9a-2ac2-58e2-a865-52a34de70b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [1, 6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b1bc666-c1ba-5ce6-9c31-2be31d7cebe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[MATH: x ∈ (- ∞,-1]∪[6, ∞)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183001} :answer-field/id #uuid "978eccf9-e40a-5c6f-8a80-aa6b0818daee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae4021eb-8552-533b-abb1-d702870385be" :question/math-academy-id "q-31079" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}\\ge 5x+6.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x+6 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x-6 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-5x-6$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-6 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/51c7484f806696105dd570684f8b194d3c1b7fc3ea27d85a1a17f53e6f7d0a64.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-5x-6\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 6.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty ).$"}]}
